                            <comment id="15510716" author="moon" created="Wed, 21 Sep 2016 18:12:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;English translation for your convenience:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An Zeppelin installation that uses JDBC interpreter to connect SQL Server, MySQL. The system runs only Zeppelin and makes a lot of large queries to those RDBMS. After some time, Zeppelin eventually slows down and becomes almost impossible to use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Restarting zeppelin daemon resolve the problem, so it looks like there are some problem on JDBC interpreter, such as memory leak, etc.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Multiple users experienced the same problem.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15511773" author="zjffdu" created="Thu, 22 Sep 2016 01:31:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;For now all the interpreter processes run in the same host of zeppelin server, I think it would be better to run them as yarn app (yarn-cluster for spark) so that we can distribute the pressure across the cluster. &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=moon&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;moon&quot;&gt;moon&lt;/a&gt; What do you think ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15511803" author="moon" created="Thu, 22 Sep 2016 01:43:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think this issue is more like some kind of slow down, hanging problem of JDBC interpreter, after long running. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But i agree, ability to run interpreter process in distributed cluster will be very useful.&lt;br/&gt;
I remember this topic has discussed in the community before and &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jongyoul&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jongyoul&quot;&gt;jongyoul&lt;/a&gt; is interested in this topic. He created a proposal related to the topic at &lt;a href=&quot;https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/ZEPPELIN/Cluster+Manager+Proposal&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/ZEPPELIN/Cluster+Manager+Proposal&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jongyoul&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jongyoul&quot;&gt;jongyoul&lt;/a&gt; why don&apos;t we discuss the design and bring this ability to Zeppelin?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15511811" author="zjffdu" created="Thu, 22 Sep 2016 01:46:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Cool, thanks for the info. Let me check the doc first. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15511863" author="jongyoul" created="Thu, 22 Sep 2016 02:16:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt; Feel free to tell me your thought about the doc. I think running interpreter in a yarn cluster should be supported. This will overcome resources&apos; limit.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
